  "slug": "mephit-fur-meet",
  "name": "Mephit Fur Meet",
  "shortName": "MFM",
  "description": "Mephit Furmeet (MFM) is an annual furry convention in the Memphis, Tennessee, area, held over the American Labor Day holiday weekend, with the motto \"Welcome home\". It was started in 1997 by Memphis furry GrowlTiger, growing out of a small pizza party at a local Howard Johnson's Inn. It is organized by the Mid-South and Tennessee Anthropomorphic Arts Association, and since Mephit Furmeet 16 it has been led by a team of five co-directors. After years at Memphis hotels, it was held at the Whispering Woods Hotel and Conference Center in Olive Branch, Mississippi, from 2010 to 2024, and then moved back to Memphis in 2025. Its charity is Tiger Haven, a big cat sanctuary, and the convention has been hosted online during the COVID-19 pandemic.",
